  FINDINGS AND OBSERVATIONS RAISED
    B-1  BENCH: swi_d has two power supplies and the session's single PDU outlet cannot
         power-cycle it. Sent as a NEEDS TEST ENGINEER: line. The framework's own
         post-failure power cycle would not power-cycle this unit either.
    MF-1 METHOD: `show log permanent | include <pattern>` never returns a prompt when the
         pattern matches nothing -- measured twice, each wait exactly equal to the
         driver's timeout, the second one long enough for the DUT's own console
         idle-timeout to fire. Prove an absence with `grep -c` on /flash/log/ instead.
    O-5  `log permanent level <lvl>` APPENDS a filter rather than changing the default
         one; the union is what takes effect. Same mechanism as T33401's finding F-1 --
         on this platform these sub-commands are filter builders, not property setters.
    M-3  NVS on this platform is /flash/log/messages on /dev/mmcblk0p1 (ext3 on the
         eMMC), rotated at each boot, holding roughly a day. The volatile log is
         /var/log/messages on a 10240k tmpfs.
    (method) There is no `show log buffered` command; the buffered log is plain `show log`.

